---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'install', label: 'Install' },
   { id: 'first-run', label: 'First run' },
   { id: 'behavior', label: 'Rules in the skill' },
   { id: 'mcp', label: 'Skill and MCP server' },
   { id: 'update', label: 'Update' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Install the agent skill"
   summary="The skill is a set of instructions that teaches a coding agent how to use a11ied: look up a criterion's test method before testing it, pick VoiceOver, NVDA, or the simulated screen reader to match the question, and report automated results and screen reader transcripts separately."
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section class="panel" id="install">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <p>
         <a href="http://aix.a1st.dev/">aix</a> finds the coding agents installed on your machine
         and asks which one gets the skill. Installing at user scope makes it available to that
         agent in every project.
      </p>
      <pre><code>npx -y @a1st/aix install https://github.com/hypothesi/a11ied/blob/master/packages/skills/ai.json --only skills --user</code></pre>
      <p>
         Add <code>--target claude-code</code>, <code>--target codex</code>, or another supported
         agent name to install without being asked.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="first-run">
      <h2>First run</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>Install the <code>a1</code> command if it is not already on the machine.</li>
         <li>Restart the coding agent so it loads the new skill.</li>
         <li>Start the app you want to test.</li>
         <li>Give it the route and the behavior you want checked.</li>
      </ol>
      <pre><code>npm install --global a11ied

a1 doctor</code></pre>
      <pre data-label="AI AGENT PROMPT"><code>Use the a11ied skill to test http://localhost:3000/checkout.
Run the automated checks first, then test the field labels and the
error messages with the screen reader. Keep the two results separate.</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger" id="behavior">
      <h2>Rules in the skill</h2>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Looks up the criterion first</strong>
            <span>When the task includes a criterion from the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG), the agent runs <code>wcag_show</code> and reads the criterion's <a href="/test-methods">test method</a> before it runs anything else.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Narrows to the relevant criteria</strong>
            <span>The agent runs <code>audit</code> and reads the list of criteria the page's structure makes <a href="/relevant-criteria">relevant</a>, instead of testing every criterion on every route.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Picks the test method</strong>
            <span>Automated when axe rules decide the criterion, hybrid when a person judges part of the result, manual when a11ied can only explain the criterion.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Moves from simulated to real</strong>
            <span>The simulated screen reader for fast local runs, VoiceOver or NVDA when the question is how the real software behaves.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Reports results separately</strong>
            <span>Automated results, transcripts, and a person's judgment stay apart in the report. A passing axe run is not reported as meeting WCAG.</span>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="mcp">
      <h2>Skill and MCP server</h2>
      <p>
         The skill tells the agent how to plan a test. The MCP server gives it the tools to run
         one. Either works without the other. With both, the agent has the tools and the
         instructions for using them.
      </p>
      <p>
         The installed instructions come from <code>packages/skills/a11ied/SKILL.md</code> in the
         repository.
      </p>
      <p>
         Follow <a href="/guides/agents">use with an AI agent</a> to connect the MCP server. Use
         the <a href="/reference/mcp">MCP reference</a> when you need exact tool inputs.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note" id="update">
      <h2>Update</h2>
      <p>
         The same <code>aix install</code> command pulls the current skill from the repository and
         reinstalls it at user scope.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
